{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -i 'release.preparation|STDO.*skill|candidate_ready|package_release|bounded' /Users/jim/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md\"","aggregated_output":"10:- rollout_summaries/2026-05-12T23-06-09-GFeP-describe_current_odd_sdlc_project.md (cwd=/Users/jim/src/apps/odd_sdlc, rollout_path=/Users/jim/.codex/sessions/2026/05/13/rollout-2026-05-13T09-06-09-019e1e70-cda1-7613-b50b-93001cca29eb.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-24T11:32:38+00:00, thread_id=019e1e70-cda1-7613-b50b-93001cca29eb, authoritative-source orientation and bounded runtime caveats)\n24:- `odd_sdlc.TS` is the governed ODD-native direction: graph functions, typed assets, replay-visible ABG truth, and bounded SDLC hooks. Treat Python as operational discovery/comparison evidence, not TypeScript architecture authority. The target is a consequence-chain loop from mutable-workspace observation and obligation binding through ranked published actions, admitted construction and bounded `F_P`, evidence admission, disposition, and replay-visible next action. [Task 1]\n30:- symptom: Python `gaps` is presented as a healthy runtime probe -> cause: `build_tenants/python/code/odd_sdlc/workspace_assets.py` contained unresolved merge markers -> fix: report the bounded failure, `SyntaxError: invalid syntax` at `<<<<<<< Updated upstream`, rather than infer runtime behavior. [Task 1]\n57:- The ontology’s recursive emergence account is: interactions produce persistent organisation; organisation changes the conditions of later interactions; those altered conditions enable further organisation. STDO is a bounded engineering instance within this broader reality-first account. [Task 1]\n61:- symptom: synthesis becomes an STDO representation/assurance account -> cause: its engineering machinery displaced the ontology’s actual subject -> fix: lead with emergence, persistence, memory, and changing transformation topology; then import STDO distinctions as bounded engineering cases. [Task 1]\n107:- Migration must classify legacy operations by evidence: established new totality/closed dependencies; pending additional evidence or bounded implementation; unresolved successor classification. An alias or stable URN cannot silently reinterpret old evidence, meaning, termination, or closed dependencies. [Task 1]\n168:scope: Use for a frozen, read-only assessment of the ABG common computational library's repair-B/D final cut, especially actual helper-to-parent failure handoff and bounded proof claims.\n191:- Final-run attribution is bounded: D retains B's files plus two additions, no new failing identity appears, and changed `identity_end` cancellation matched standalone reruns. Do not generalize this to unrun suites. [Task 1]\n287:scope: Use for evidence-bounded local Rival saved-variable comparisons, current Forever class identity research, or practical Enhancement leveling advice.\n324:# Task Group: specification_methodology v3/a_c candidate and release-preparation reviews\n326:scope: Use for read-only checkpoint, Graphify/a_c transport, or common-representation release-bundle review; retain strict distinctions between bounded checks, semantic acceptance, qualification, publication, and release.\n333:- rollout_summaries/2026-10-14T18-17-13-h1OE-read_only_review_v3_a_c_common_representation_release_gaps.md (cwd=/Users/jim, rollout_path=/Users/jim/.codex/sessions/2026/10/15/rollout-2026-10-15T05-17-13-01a13ba1-fbf0-7a90-a7c8-4f49576f5bf0.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-20T12:56:37+00:00, thread_id=01a13ba1-fbf0-7a90-a7c8-4f49576f5bf0, clean `candidate_ready` checkpoint, not accepted/released)\n337:- candidate_ready, C3 iteration-3, c29b2be37f9a12e050478be97793927d99c01781, 30/30 assertions, T2 replay, qualification reader, concurrency race\n339:## Task 2: Review common v3 representation release preparation, partial\n347:- stdo-v3-common-35fb4824, bundle_check.py, package_release.py, public_receipts.py, `--dist`, `--bundle`, SOURCE-READINESS.md, source_commit, package_tree, HTML-unverified\n351:- when reviewing work called “complete” or `candidate_ready` -> preserve candidate construction, independent evidence, owner acceptance, integrated qualification, publication, and release as separate states. [Task 1]\n352:- when reviewing release preparation marked `not_ready`, uncommitted/unpublished, or acceptance-pending -> preserve those boundaries even if custody and package checks pass. [Task 2]\n357:- Candidate checkpoint `c29b2be37f9a12e050478be97793927d99c01781` had bounded evidence (63 dispositions, 89 members, 30/30 assertions, T2 replay 6/6), but same-family/non-author evidence, context fit, owner decisions, installed qualification, C3 acceptance, and release were open. The locked successor reader fixed counter controls but did not retroactively qualify original attempts. [Task 1]\n358:- The common archive passed bounded custody/portable verification and exact recovery, but remained locally reviewable with `semantic_acceptance: not_issued`, `publication: not_performed`, actual-use unperformed, and HTML interaction unverified. [Task 2]\n387:- The I3 common contract requires foundations to govern actual decisions, inherited deciding rules to remain covered, domain results to retain predicates and determining conditions, and contraction to preserve permissions, scope, modal force, triggers, exceptions, and authority. `REPAIR RETURNED`, `BOUNDED EVIDENCE`, `RESERVED`, and `OPEN` are work-list states, not acceptance. [Task 1]\n426:scope: Use for read-only review of ABIogenesis transformation-library proposals, process/effect finalization, or an evidence-bounded RC1 status; preserve the distinction between proposal, source/component findings, installed qualification, and release readiness.\n450:- `worksite_command_helper.ts::runHttpProbe` can report `terminationConfirmed:true` after launcher close without proving the owned POSIX process group is absent. Reuse the existing group probe and bounded TERM/grace/KILL confirmation path; keep Windows child-process behavior separate. [Task 1]\n451:- Product.resolve phase231 remains an unlocalized capacity blocker: stock V8 heap aborted after 266.124 seconds before a resolve result, with no established allocating owner or dominant retainer. Do not attribute cause or retry without a new bounded activation. Earlier graph validation, Testing/UAT source eligibility, BOM, declaration-comparison, failed-child propagation, and bounded evidence-reuse repairs held only in inspected source/component scope; installed qualification and RC1 release remain open. [Task 1]\n478:- rollout_summaries/2026-09-29T15-14-42-7gWO-abiogenesis_consumer_reuse_repair_accepted_rc1_open.md (cwd=/Users/jim/src/apps, rollout_path=/Users/jim/.codex/sessions/2026/09/30/rollout-2026-09-30T01-14-42-01a0edbb-7c4f-7493-bf06-2a600644bbb6.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-05T02:00:55+00:00, thread_id=01a0edbb-7c4f-7493-bf06-2a600644bbb6, independently accepted bounded consumer-preparation/recovery cut)\n497:- when a bounded run hit an integration/oracle mismatch -> stop at the first failure, preserve the failed cut, correct only the owning caller/test, and obtain independent review rather than blindly retrying or changing the framework. [Task 2]\n498:- when reporting progress -> distinguish component preparation and bounded runtime evidence from Public qualification, semantic acceptance, F11/AF22, and release readiness. [Task 2][Task 3]\n512:- symptom: a dirty checkout or bounded acceptance is treated as a frozen release subject or RC1 readiness -> cause: the exact subject and qualification boundary were not bound -> fix: preserve unrelated work, name/freeze the cut, and state the remaining Public/F11/AF22/release work explicitly. [Task 1][Task 3]\n516:scope: Use for bounded `odd_manager` integration with a frozen ABIogenesis 5 observation contract, independent qualification of the Run Inspector slice, or a requested full-worktree checkpoint/push.\n523:- rollout_summaries/2026-09-29T01-19-34-5ppk-odd_manager_abg5_rc1_alignment_and_full_checkpoint_push.md (cwd=/Users/jim/src/apps, rollout_path=/Users/jim/.codex/sessions/2026/09/29/rollout-2026-09-29T11-19-34-01a0eabe-e5c6-79e1-b675-e5613a34a07e.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-29T13:01:00+00:00, thread_id=01a0eabe-e5c6-79e1-b675-e5613a34a07e, accepted bounded current-run observation slice)\n547:- `odd_manager` owns bounded admission/read models and operator presentation; ABIogenesis owns events, replay semantics, Run truth, and liveness. The slice supplies identity-first discovery, per-Run status, bounded event pages, and lazy call detail. Key seams: `build_tenants/react_vite/src/server/abg-event-carrier-service.mjs`, `retained-run-observation-service.mjs`, `src/contracts/abg-run-observation.ts`, browser ingress validation, and `runtime/tests/test_t046_current_run_observation.mjs`. [Task 1]\n554:- symptom: I-01 evidence is reported as broad ABIogenesis 5 or odd_glc-on-5 compatibility -> cause: bounded frozen-profile qualification was overgeneralized -> fix: retain explicit residuals: `a25/current_intent`, native liveness, I-02/I-03 richer projections, and I-04 remain unqualified. [Task 1]\n582:- `REQ-28`–`REQ-33` and falsifiers `S-29`–`S-34` are open framework obligations. The PoC reports bounded economic results and must not claim commercial edge, full component admission/substitution, complete external execution lifecycle, persistent assurance records, or independent regulatory verification. [Task 1]\n587:- symptom: a broad modular framework is described as already realized -> cause: bounded PoC coverage is mistaken for full framework assurance -> fix: mark open obligations and falsifiers explicitly, and retain the separation between the four findings. [Task 1]\n1085:scope: Use for independent STDO v3 tenant review and non-authoritative commentary criteria; protect peer isolation, common authority, semantic assessment, and bounded evaluation decisions.\n1112:- when the user says “i want you to post this as review criteria” -> create a bounded `.ai-workspace/comments/<agent>/` commentary artifact, not merely chat prose. [Task 2]\n1122:- Proposed probes are the neutral sum-and-histogram categorical steel thread, uncertain-effect recovery, and bounded ordinary triage/ticket/release tasks using a common oracle and selected frames. The proposed 90-minute-per-assessor/USD-10 envelope and reported ~32,600-token scratch experiment remain proposal/exploratory evidence, not an authorized spend grant or qualification. [Task 2]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
