{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '324,358p' /Users/jim/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Task Group: specification_methodology v3/a_c candidate and release-preparation reviews\n\nscope: Use for read-only checkpoint, Graphify/a_c transport, or common-representation release-bundle review; retain strict distinctions between bounded checks, semantic acceptance, qualification, publication, and release.\napplies_to: cwd=/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology; reuse_rule=safe for the review method and named defect patterns; exact hashes, paths, counts, and release status are time-specific.\n\n## Task 1: Review Codex v3 iteration-3 candidate checkpoint, success\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-10-14T18-17-13-h1OE-read_only_review_v3_a_c_common_representation_release_gaps.md (cwd=/Users/jim, rollout_path=/Users/jim/.codex/sessions/2026/10/15/rollout-2026-10-15T05-17-13-01a13ba1-fbf0-7a90-a7c8-4f49576f5bf0.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-20T12:56:37+00:00, thread_id=01a13ba1-fbf0-7a90-a7c8-4f49576f5bf0, clean `candidate_ready` checkpoint, not accepted/released)\n\n### keywords\n\n- candidate_ready, C3 iteration-3, c29b2be37f9a12e050478be97793927d99c01781, 30/30 assertions, T2 replay, qualification reader, concurrency race\n\n## Task 2: Review common v3 representation release preparation, partial\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-10-14T18-17-13-h1OE-read_only_review_v3_a_c_common_representation_release_gaps.md (cwd=/Users/jim, rollout_path=/Users/jim/.codex/sessions/2026/10/15/rollout-2026-10-15T05-17-13-01a13ba1-fbf0-7a90-a7c8-4f49576f5bf0.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-20T12:56:37+00:00, thread_id=01a13ba1-fbf0-7a90-a7c8-4f49576f5bf0, portable checks passed; three packaging defects found)\n\n### keywords\n\n- stdo-v3-common-35fb4824, bundle_check.py, package_release.py, public_receipts.py, `--dist`, `--bundle`, SOURCE-READINESS.md, source_commit, package_tree, HTML-unverified\n\n## User preferences\n\n- when reviewing work called “complete” or `candidate_ready` -> preserve candidate construction, independent evidence, owner acceptance, integrated qualification, publication, and release as separate states. [Task 1]\n- when reviewing release preparation marked `not_ready`, uncommitted/unpublished, or acceptance-pending -> preserve those boundaries even if custody and package checks pass. [Task 2]\n- when the user says “stop” after a wrong paste -> halt immediately, make no edits/commits, and confirm Git/filesystem state. [Task 1]\n\n## Reusable knowledge\n\n- Candidate checkpoint `c29b2be37f9a12e050478be97793927d99c01781` had bounded evidence (63 dispositions, 89 members, 30/30 assertions, T2 replay 6/6), but same-family/non-author evidence, context fit, owner decisions, installed qualification, C3 acceptance, and release were open. The locked successor reader fixed counter controls but did not retroactively qualify original attempts. [Task 1]\n- The common archive passed bounded custody/portable verification and exact recovery, but remained locally reviewable with `semantic_acceptance: not_issued`, `publication: not_performed`, actual-use unperformed, and HTML interaction unverified. [Task 2]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"for f in basis.md tools.md release-install.md; do printf '\\\\nFILE %s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$f\"; cat \".agents/skills/stdo-work/references/$f\"; done'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"for f in basis.md tools.md release-install.md; do printf '\\\\nFILE %s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$f\"; cat \".agents/skills/stdo-work/references/$f\"; done'","aggregated_output":"\nFILE basis.md\n# Bind the exact workspace and method\n\nRun the manager on the selected target Product Definition, not this package's construction definition by default:\n\n```sh\nstdo status --definition /absolute/path/to/selected-product.json --verify\n```\n\nInspect the actual result: installed, valid, failures, definition identity, basis, manifest and installed path. This candidate supports exactly `stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/`, manifest `60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8`. A channel is discovery, never adoption. Missing install, changed member, ambiguous Product or another cut withholds dependent work; name the missing premise and its owner. Setup may install/pin only where its operation grant permits, using the manager's discovered supported contract. Do not guess a setup command.\n\nResolve the definition's declared bootstrap from the verified installed path. For an already activated step, do not reload the whole method. Acquire the deciding sections for the task through the selected source.read contract. [Source routes](../source-routes.json) retain exact common/host/tool provenance for this package; root names are resolved by the active policy, not silently rebound to a sibling.\n\n| Decision | Owner in the exact installation's standards directory |\n|---|---|\n| Product selection and install | PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md §§2, 4, 7, 9, 12 |\n| WHAT/HOW and tenant | SPEC_METHOD.md §§2, 11; PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md §8 |\n| Intake, existing authority and admission | ACTIVATION.md §1 |\n| Bounded context and exact activation | ACTIVATION.md §2; REFERENCE_FRAME.md §§3, 11 |\n| Result and effect | ACTIVATION.md §3; AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md §§5, 7 |\n| Executive/Worker roles | EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md §§6, 8–10, 12, 16–19 |\n| Independent review | EVALUATION.md §§3, 5, 7 |\n| Recovery/currentness | ACTIVATION.md §§5, 7; FOUNDATIONS.md observation sufficiency |\n| Proportional proof | ACTIVATION.md §6 and transition evidence |\n| Actual path | ASSURANCE.md §§7–9; EVALUATION.md §7 |\n| Release/adoption | RELEASE.md; IDENTITY.md |\n\nThese are routes, not copied law. Use the manager's verified member hashes and exact SourceRefs; select the needed lines only after locating the section in that member. Read changed-owner source before changing realization. Preserve higher meaning unless its owner actually authorizes change. The package cannot adopt or repair its immutable method.\n\nRecord the relevant host version, resolved model/effort when observable, tool implementation and method profile. HOST.md identifies codex-cli 0.164.0 mechanics for this candidate; it does not prove any run's resolved model. Missing usage/model evidence remains unknown.\n\nFILE tools.md\n# Public tool path\n\nUse the operation implementation selected by the target Product/activation. The construction binding is `urn:a-c:fd-support:method:stdo-3.0.1-rc.1:executive:1`, SHA256 `a886047e50b8a45c3b47addea0f0809dca2a6c54ac35948df5e01893cc30bbf7`. Its legacy builder identity is separate. Native results.conjoin is unsupported; never relabel a legacy conjunction.\n\nThe ordinary public CLI is sufficient. Supply an exact policy, its digest and the authorized principal; inherit the environment. For this construction the observed executable is Python 3.13.7 and the entrypoint is `/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py`. Resolve that development-tool installation explicitly in another workspace. Do not assume a portable absolute path.\n\nThis executable transport pattern reads an envelope from stdin, creates no request file and preserves the CLI's response:\n\n```sh\n\"$AC_PYTHON\" -B \"$AC_ENTRY\" --policy \"$AC_POLICY\" \\\n  --policy-sha256 \"$AC_POLICY_SHA256\" --principal \"$AC_PRINCIPAL\" \\\n  call --request - <<'JSON'\n{\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\",\"id\":\"describe-work-write-unique\",\"operation\":\"tools.describe\",\"arguments\":{\"operation\":\"work.write\"}}\nJSON\n```\n\nSet AC_PYTHON, AC_ENTRY, AC_POLICY, AC_POLICY_SHA256 and AC_PRINCIPAL from the active tool binding, not example authority. Use a distinct request id for each new operation. Reuse acquired schemas while their basis is current. Inspect status, refusal, result, operation_outcome and evidence. Save actual responses through the authorized evidence mechanism; a successful process exit is not a semantic verdict.\n\nAcquisition envelope arguments:\n```json\n{\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"root\":\"method\",\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"object\":null,\"sha256\":\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[1004,1055]}},\"encoding\":\"utf8\"}\n```\nUse operation `source.read` in the same envelope. Root aliases and access must exist in the selected policy. Preserve parent/selected digests and acquisition evidence.\n\nFor an authorized write:\n1. Ensure the containing directory exists through an explicitly granted mechanism. If mkdir is allowed, reject symlinks and path escape. No directory permission can be inferred from file permission.\n2. Call `workspace.observe` with `{\"scope\":[{\"root\":\"product\",\"path\":\"the/containing/directory\",\"kind\":\"directory\"}]}`. Retain its result.artifact; do not substitute the response evidence for the observation.\n3. Call `work.write` using the exact returned input schema: grant_id; target SourceRef with exact preimage digest (null only when absent); mode \"replace\" or the granted append; record {text, provenance}; interpretation null unless declared; observations [the fresh observation artifact]. Provenance is the actual authority source.\n4. Retain the returned postimage, effect scope, result artifact and OperationEvidence. Check that the postimage matches intended bytes. No further dependent effect after uncertainty until reconciliation.\n\nFor `evidence.read`, arguments are `{\"artifact\":{\"id\":\"sha256:…\",\"sha256\":\"…\"}}`; supply the real returned digest. The ellipsis here denotes a required observed value, not an executable request.\n\nFor context, admission, review or dispatch use `tools.describe` for the named operation and current method_profile, then construct its exact input from the active contract. Discovery is not authority. If the required operation or binding is unsupported, preserve the real refusal and return the required capability/owner; do not invoke a substitute and claim the original path passed. An F_P assessment is authored evidence, not a deterministic tool predicate. Native Executive consumption must retain all required evaluations, applicability uncertainty, incompatible bases and contradictions; it cannot fabricate a qualified join.\n\nAuxiliary host reads/hashes/read-only validators establish finite byte facts only. Any host mutation requires its own declared operation grant and actual-path qualification; it never stands in for a required tool result.\n\nFILE release-install.md\n# Release preparation and scoped deployment\n\nAcquire RELEASE.md and IDENTITY.md from the verified installation and the target Product's release conditions. Bind exact candidate inventory, evidence, acceptance/disposition requirements, destination and publication grant. With a preparation-only grant, assemble a reviewable local artifact and return it; no remote publication follows. Do not invent a second final cut to fix an identity problem. Discover and actually use the release tool contract selected by that Product; unsupported release tooling leaves publication unperformed.\n\nThis skill's deployment unit is the entire stdo-work directory. Its repository-local destination is exactly TARGET/.agents/skills/stdo-work. It neither installs the Claude tenant nor modifies host defaults. The tenant README documents the executable package verifier and copy recipe. At deployment time:\n1. Freeze the package inventory, verify all ordinary regular files and internal resources, and retain the chosen identity outside the discovery directory.\n2. Verify the target grant and every destination ancestor: no symlink, escape or unexpected existing stdo-work. Resolve duplicate skill names deliberately; names are not merged.\n3. Install only that directory. Record destination, exact file inventory and old/new package identities in the authorized work surface.\n4. Open Codex in that workspace. Exercise ordinary discovery and explicit $stdo-work invocation as separate trials. Confirm acquisition and required tool events. If stale, restart and retain the failed discovery attempt.\n5. For update, compare the entire installed file set and hashes to the retained old receipt before replacement. If locally changed or ownership unknown, stop that replacement and report the conflict; do not overwrite it. Retain the old package outside all discovery roots and its identity for deliberate rollback.\n6. Remove only the owned selected stdo-work directory after the same receipt check. Preserve .agents/skills, other skills and configuration. Unknown files or hashes block destructive removal. Recheck the remaining unrelated configuration.\n\nThese instructions specify a deployable path. Finite package checks do not prove discovery, actual installation, update or removal behavior; Q12 remains open until performed in an authorized disposable host workspace. Installation does not constitute method adoption or Product acceptance.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
